WEBVTT

00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:13,470
Can a person take too much vitamin D? Yes, you can.

00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:21,470
Matter of fact, it's hard to discern sometimes because some labs won't measure the total vitamin D.

00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:27,710
They'll just say greater than 150 on your labs. So it's like, well, what do you mean?

00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:34,990
Is it 160 or is it 600? Well, some labs don't give you the exact number beyond

00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:45,550
a specific number, like 150. Now personally, under the belief that it would be good for somebody

00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:54,350
with cancer to have a vitamin D level of 80 to 150. However, when you get vitamin D levels up

00:00:54,350 --> 00:01:00,910
to 300 because you're taking 20,000 IUs a day and you have for the last five years and you don't have

00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:09,230
VDR defects in your genes, you're absorbing a lot of vitamin D that you're taking and you could

00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:14,750
have elevated vitamin D levels. That's why I suggest people get their vitamin D levels tested.

00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:22,830
If it is beyond 200, I don't suggest you continue taking

00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:29,710
oral vitamin D. So yes, I do think there can be dangers in too much vitamin D.

00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:36,270
Is there any data that shows vitamin D toxicity? There's just a few papers in the literature

00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:42,750
back from I think the 1980s where somebody was taking high dose vitamin D for a period of time and

00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:50,030
they did have vitamin D toxicity. But anything can be too much of a good thing, can be a bad thing.

00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:57,950
So yes, I do think that a person can get too much of anything. So vitamin D is one of those things.

00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:04,270
So I don't take a person should be taking 25,000 IUs a vitamin D constantly without getting

00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:10,750
their vitamin D levels checked. If you're taking 5,000 IUs a vitamin D on a daily basis, you're never

00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:17,710
going to have too much vitamin D. It's the people that are taking 20 to 25 I've had talked to people

00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:24,190
that were taking 50,000 IUs a vitamin D a day because they saw some Instagram video of somebody saying

00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:30,350
that that was good for you. Well, anything is where you just got to be careful. There's

00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:39,710
anybody could go on Instagram that isn't a practitioner or maybe a retired practitioner. They can say

00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:48,350
all sorts of things that don't get them into trouble because they're not technically a practitioner.

00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:54,750
They're not licensed any longer. So if somebody follows their advice via a video on Instagram,

00:02:54,750 --> 00:03:03,470
they're not going to be held liable. But I think you're morally liable. That's what bothers me about

00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:11,230
Instagram and this not because it seems like these people are just saying things in order to get

00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:17,150
just hints and to get followers. And I think there's danger in that. They're going to bring that up

00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:21,470
again and a quite other question that somebody has down here. So

